      "scope": "This market covers finished urea (granular, prilled, and liquid urea) sold as a nitrogen fertilizer commodity, valued at the point it leaves the producer or is supplied through distribution, whether destined for agricultural application or industrial/technical use such as urea-ammonium nitrate solutions, DEF/AdBlue, and urea-based resins. Upstream inputs (natural gas, ammonia, carbon dioxide, hydrogen) are excluded as separately valued commodities and are treated only as cost/intensity drivers, while downstream outcomes such as crop yields, harvested grain, and finished industrial end-products are likewise outside the market boundary. Downstream end-use demand (e.g., wheat or cereal acreage and application rates, DEF consumption, resin production volumes) is not itself valued here but is used as an intermediate signal to derive how much urea those usages require. Urea used as an animal feed additive or in non-fertilizer pharmaceutical/cosmetic applications is included only where it is the same finished urea commodity; unrelated nitrogen products (ammonium nitrate, UAN blends priced as distinct products, ammonia) are out of scope.",
